Label $a = t, b = u,..$, then \begin{align*}\sum_{cyc}^{a^8} = a^8 + b^8 + c^8 + d^8= (\sum_{cyc}^{a^4})^2 &- 2(\sum_{cyc}^{a^4b^4})\tag*{bezout}\\&-2\sum_{cyc}^{a^4bc}\tag*{amexpli}\\&-2\sum_{cyc}^{a^2b^2}\tag*{bhwtrc}\\&-2\sum_{cyc}^{ab}\tag*{?=2} \\&-4abcd\tag*{uvw}\\&+ 4(a^4b^4 + a^4c^4 +a^4d^4+b^4c^4+ b^4d^4 + c^4d^4)\end{align*}> <answer> As you probably know, the equality follows as:
\begin{align*}
(a+b+c+d)(a^3+b^3+c^3+d^3) =\sum_{sym}^{abcd} a^3\cdot b^1 =  \prod_{sym}^{abcd} a^1 = a^4 + b^4 + c^4 + d^4 + 2\sum_{sym}^{abcd} a^3\cdot b^1 =  (a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2)^2 \tag*{bezout}\end{align*}
The first equality follows from AM–GM and the triangle inequality, while the equality to be proved follows directly.$\quad\blacksquare$
</answer>
